### 1. High — `apps/ai-hero/docs/quiz.md` identity section (~line 74)

The doc claims the same authored `id` in two different lessons "cannot
collide" because the endpoint resolves through the lesson join. Macroscope
says `targetResourceId(bindingId, 'question', authoredId)` has no lesson
component, so the minted resource id is per-**binding**, not per-lesson.

Verify in `apps/ai-hero/src/course-sync/control-plane.ts` (and
`quiz-question-extraction.ts`): what actually happens when two lessons in the
SAME course binding reuse one authored question id? Trace it — do both lessons
attach the same `sync_question_<hash>` resource? Does the second sync
overwrite the first's `fields` (question text, `correct`,
`courseSync.sourceLessonId`)? Does extraction or the control plane reject it
anywhere? Then rewrite the identity paragraph and, if the behavior is a silent
overwrite, add it to the doc's sharp-edges list. State what is true: the
uniqueness scope of an authored id, what the lesson join in the endpoint does
and does not protect, and what an author must not do.

### 2. Medium — `.brain/projects/quiz-component/decide-multi-select-in-the-inline-quiz.svx` (~line 71)

The receipt shows a `gradeAnswer` snippet whose scalar branch uses strict
